(k=n-t\\) we obtain  \n\n   \\[\n   k=0,1,\\dots ,\\,n-\\tau(n)=\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{n}{3}\\Bigr\\rfloor .\n   \\]\n\n   For each such \\(k\\) an explicit construction is obtained by the covering used in the upper‑bound part of Lemma 1 (which uses exactly \\(\\tau(n)\\) non‑sunny lines) together with \\(n-\\tau(n)-k\\) additional diagonal lines (still non‑sunny) and finally \\(k\\) arbitrary sunny lines of distinct irrational slopes.\n\n**Conclusion.**  \nAll non‑negative integers \\(k\\) satisfying  \n\n\\[\n0\\le k\\le\\left\\lfloor\\frac{n}{3}\\right\\rfloor\n\\]\n\nand only those admit a configuration of \\(n\\) distinct lines meeting the two conditions of the problem. ∎"
