, non‑sunny, and they cover all points of \\(T_n\\) whose first\ncoordinate satisfies \\(a\\le r\\).\n\n**(ii) Points still uncovered.**  \nDefine  \n\n\\[\nU:=\\{(a,b)\\in T_n\\mid r+1\\le a\\le n\\}\n   =\\bigl\\{(r+s,\\;b)\\mid 1\\le s\\le k,\\;1\\le b\\le k+1-s\\bigr\\}.\n\\tag{8}\n\\]\n\nThe set \\(U\\) is a right‑angled triangular array containing exactly\n\\(\\displaystyle\\frac{k(k+1)}2\\) lattice points.\n\n**(iii) Sunny lines covering \\(U\\).**  \nFor each \\(s=1,2,\\dots ,k\\) define  \n\n\\[\nL_s:\\;y = x - (r+s) + (k+1-s)\n      \\;=\\;x - r -2s +k+1 .\n\\tag{9}\n\\]\n\nThe slope of \\(L_s\\) is \\(1\\); therefore \\(L_s\\) is sunny (it is not parallel\nto the \\(x\\)-axis, the \\(y\\)-axis nor to \\(x+y=0\\)).  \nA direct substitution shows that the integer points of \\(U\\) lying on \\(L_s\\) are  \n\n\\[\n\\bigl\\{(r+s+i-1,\\;i)\\mid i=1,2,\\dots ,k+1-s\\bigr\\},\n\\tag{10}\n\\]\ni.e. the whole \\(s\\)-th column of the triangle.  Consequently  \n\n\\[\n|L_s\\cap U| = k+1-s .\n\\]\n\nThe \\(k\\) lines \\(L_1,\\dots ,L_k\\) are distinct because their intercepts\n\\(-r-2s+k+1\\) are different.  Moreover,\n\\[\n\\bigcup_{s=1}^{k} (L_s\\cap U)=U .\n\\]\n\n**(iv) Verification.**  \nThe total number of lines used is \\(r+(k)=n\\); all are distinct.  \nEvery point of \\(T_n\\) belongs either to a vertical line from (7) (if its first\ncoordinate \\(\\le r\\)) or to one of the sunny lines \\(L_s\\) (if its first\ncoordinate \\(>r\\)).  Hence both conditions of the problem are satisfied.\n\n**(v) Extremal values.**  \n\n* \\(k=0\\): take the \\(n\\) vertical lines \\(x=1,\\dots ,x=n\\).  \n* \\(n\\) odd, \\(k=n\\): then \\(r=0\\) and the construction reduces to the family\n  \\(\\{L_s\\}_{s=1}^{n}\\), which indeed covers all of \\(T_n\\).  \n* \\(n\\) even, \\(k=n-1\\): then \\(r=1\\); we use the single vertical line \\(x=1\\)\n  together with the \\(n-1\\) sunny lines \\(L_s\\) (\\(s=1,\\dots ,n-1\\)).\n\nThus for **every** integer \\(k\\) satisfying (6) we have exhibited a concrete\nconfiguration of \\(n\\) distinct lines with exactly \\(k\\) sunny ones.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 4.  Final answer  \n\nCombining the necessary bound (6) with the explicit construction, we obtain that\nthe admissible values of \\(k\\) are precisely those described in (★).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;0\\le k\\le \n\\begin{cases}\nn      &\\text{if }n\\text{ is odd},\\\\[2mm]\nn-1    &\\text{if }n\\text{ is even}.\n\\end{cases}}\\qquad\\blacksquare\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
